3. The brief facts of the present case are that on 15.03.2008, the Food Inspector Sh. Dharam Pal Singh, Food Assistant Sh. D.N. Verma, under the supervision of Local Health Authority/SDM Sh.
S.S. Parihar reached at the premises of M/s Sarvan Store at Bharthal Road near Bijwasan Railway Station, Bijwasan, New Delhi, where accused/appellant was found conducting his business of CA no.
263/16 Sarvan Vs. Delhi Admn /Food Inspector (PFA) Pages 2 of 13 various food articles which were lying stored for sale for human consumption ;
- that FI disclosed his identity and expressed his intention to purchase a sample of 'Moong Dal Chilka' from the vendor which was lying in open gunny bag bearing no label declaration, to which he agreed ;
- that thereafter as per the prescribed procedure under the PFA Act and Rules after giving notice to the vendor/appellant and offer towards sale price of sample to which he agreed and accept, sample was then lifted ; that sample was separately packed, fastened, marked, sealed and necessary documents including Notice as per Form-VI in the presence of appellant/accused, panchnama etc was prepared at the spot ; that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA)
in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 02.04.2009, PA found the sample to be adulterated on the ground that it was coloured with synthetic colouring matter "Tartrazine and Brilliant Blue FCF" ;
- that upon receipt of report, SDM/LHA directed investigation which was carried out by FI and after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.

The complaint was then filed in the court on 14.03.2000 alleging violation of Section 2(ia)(a),(j) and (m) of PFA Act, as punishable under Section 7/16(1)(A) of PFA. Act.
- that the complaint was filed in writing by a public servant, hence, recording of pre-summoning evidence was dispensed with ;
CA no. 263/16 Sarvan Vs. Delhi Admn /Food Inspector (PFA) Pages 3 of 13 4.
